{# The prev/next pair for one `.carousel` -- C20 (#420). Written once and
   included by every strip rather than three copies, since the markup and
   the classes global.js binds to never vary by page.

   Sits right here, right after the strip -- the same place Kayak's own
   reference puts its pair, below the card row rather than beside its
   title. `.carousel__nav`'s own CSS hides it until global.js has proven
   there is something to scroll to, and gates it either way to
   `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)` -- touch and trackpad already drag
   the strip, so the buttons exist only for the pointer type that had no
   way in at all. #}
<div class="carousel__nav js-carousel-nav">
    <button type="button" class="carousel__arrow carousel__arrow--prev js-carousel-prev" aria-label="Scroll left">
        <i class="fas fa-chevron-left" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="carousel__arrow carousel__arrow--next js-carousel-next" aria-label="Scroll right">
        <i class="fas fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
</div>
